  "source_caveat": "DBnomics retrieves BEA-origin GDPbyIndustry Table 16 annual Chain-Type Quantity Indexes for Gross Output by Industry for NAICS 484 truck transportation. The 2026 September BEA table release was indexed by the third-party DBnomics provider on October 1, 2026. Direct publicly accessible DBnomics API returned one 484-A annual series with 2017 index 100.000 and 2024 108.047, +8.05 percent real gross output. DBnomics HTTP provenance does NOT authenticate an original BEA-supplied numeric file, BEA API authenticated request or direct BEA publisher response, and cannot be marketed as direct BEA original verification. BEA real gross output differs from BLS sectoral output (+4.02 percent, excludes intra-industry transactions), BEA GDP/value added, and the illustrative Census nominal revenue divided by BLS annual producer price index proxy (+1.18 percent); differences of 4.03 and 6.87 percentage points are descriptive, not validated statistical model error, official decomposition, customer paid freight invoice costs, real shipment tonnage, recoverable carrier overcharges or market size. Parent NAICS 484 includes long-distance TL and LTL child industries, which cannot be summed as disjoint markets. All 18 independent real-customer pilot gates remain unresolved."
